948	From Fig.~\ref{DevALRtheta-2}, we find that the deviation in differential LR asymmetry for $e^-e^+ \to \mu^+ \mu^-$ process for $x_H=-2$ is slightly above the theoretically estimated statistical error for $\cos\theta > 0.37$; however, for $x_H=-1$ it is within the range of the statistical error. For $x_H=1$ and $2$, the deviations vary between $5\%-3\%$ and $10\%-8\%$ respectively for $-1 \leq \cos\theta \leq 1$. The deviations increase with $\sqrt{s}$. The differential LR asymmetry is negative for $x_H=2$ at $\sqrt{s}=3$ TeV which is reflected in the deviation of the differential LR asymmetry as well.
